window.RULE_DIALOGUES = {"meetings": [{"id": "m1", "title": "VCS Q&A · Succession (Cont.)", "date": "", "audio": "audio/m1.m4a", "turns": [{"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "I don't have anything because we we don't do any of it ourselves for succession. Yeah, we can Compliance has access to that stuff. They can probably show you something. I don't have anything but I'm sure we can Do some research in parallel", "pol": "I don't have anything because we don't do any of it ourselves for Succession. Compliance has access to that stuff — they can probably show you something. I don't have anything, but I'm sure we can do some research in parallel.", "zh": "我这边没有资料，因为Succession的这些我们自己都不做。合规部门能访问那些东西——他们大概能给你看一些。我没有，但我确信我们可以同时做点研究。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 52.82, "e": 69.88}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Do it? I think it's a good idea to do it on a VCS. Code generator cat reporting as well, right? In which form? Yeah, that's separate. They do it separately. We cannot see them. No. We can only see, we see in the portal, like when we connect to the portal, we can just see a record that it happened. A record showing code generator cat reporting.", "pol": "I think it's a good idea to do it on VCL. Coda generates CAT reporting as well, right? In which form? Yeah, that's separate — they do it separately. We can't see them. We can only see it in the portal: when we connect to the portal, we can just see a record that it happened — a record showing Coda generated the CAT reporting.", "zh": "我觉得在VCL上做是个好主意。Coda也会生成CAT上报，对吧？以什么形式？那是分开的——他们单独做。我们看不到。我们只能在门户里看到：连上门户后，只能看到“发生过”的一条记录——一条显示Coda生成了CAT上报的记录。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 116.79, "e": 143.38}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "and then that's it nothing else the record the succession did and then if they're not matching then we would see records out as well like we don't we're not the ones actually doing it does this portal does it by itself do the reconciliation it just a equals to yeah it'll just tell you if something yeah it'll tell you there's something that's not breaking", "pol": "And that's it, nothing else — just the record of what Succession did. If they don't match, we'd see that recorded as well. We're not the ones actually doing it; this portal does it by itself, doing the reconciliation (A equals B). It'll just tell you if something isn't matching.", "zh": "就这些，没别的了——只是Succession所做的记录。如果不匹配，我们也会看到相应记录。我们并不是真正执行的人；这个门户自己完成对账（A 等于 B）。它只会告诉你是否有什么对不上。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 143.99, "e": 166.6}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "I think they said, I'm not sure because we don't do it, but I imagine it's either a file or maybe it's like a fixed message. I don't know. Something along those lines.", "pol": "I'm not sure, because we don't do it, but I imagine it's either a file or maybe a FIX message — something along those lines.", "zh": "我不确定，因为我们不做这个，但我猜要么是文件，要么是类似FIX消息之类的东西。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 190.54, "e": 207.73}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So we don't know if, because you said something here, I don't know the format. No, I don't. But compliance ones? I don't even think they know. They can, we've never done it ourselves, that's the thing. So I don't really have any... So the only thing we see right now is... We just see if there's a break or not.", "pol": "We don't know the format. Compliance? I don't even think they know either — we've never done it ourselves, that's the thing. So the only thing we see right now is whether there's a break or not.", "zh": "我们不知道格式。合规？我觉得他们也不清楚——毕竟我们自己从没做过。所以现在我们唯一能看到的，就是有没有对账异常。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 305.38, "e": 324.83}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "It's on the four boards. This one, this one, looks the same. Yes.", "pol": "It's on the dashboards. This one and this one look the same. Yes.", "zh": "它在仪表盘上。这个和这个看起来一样。是的。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 325.7, "e": 338.47}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "I'm sure if we did some research, we could figure it out by logging into this research online. I'm sure we could figure it out. Yeah. Because we haven't done it ourselves. Can we do that? Because if we replace the issue.", "pol": "I'm sure if we did some research, we could figure it out by logging into the system online. Because we haven't done it ourselves. Can we do that? Because if we replace the system...", "zh": "我确信只要做点研究、登录这个在线系统，我们就能搞清楚。毕竟我们自己没做过。我们能这么做吗？因为如果我们替换系统的话……", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 347.25, "e": 368.32}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "I think it's real time. It might not be real time. It could be a file. I'm not sure. This one is personal. Yes.", "pol": "I think it's real time — it might not be real time. It could be a file, I'm not sure. This one is personal. Yes.", "zh": "我觉得是实时的——也可能不是实时。也可能是文件，我不确定。这个是个人的。是的。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 376.45, "e": 385.29}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Is that required by someone? Yeah, it is. It's required. Does that need to be confirmed? No, no, no, no. Because on succession, they're not going to remember.", "pol": "Is that required by someone? Yeah, it's required. Does it need to be confirmed? No — because on Succession, they're not going to remember.", "zh": "这是某方要求的吗？是的，是必需的。需要确认吗？不用——因为在Succession上，他们不会记得。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 420.34, "e": 430.31}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Yeah, so there's, I think there's something called an IMID, there's something called an FDID, and then MPID, and I think all three of those things are reported by succession.", "pol": "Yeah, so there's something called an IMID, something called an FDID, and then MPID — and I think all three of those are reported by Succession.", "zh": "是的，有一个叫IMID的，一个叫FDID的，还有MPID——我认为这三个都是由Succession上报的。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 436.02, "e": 457.52}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "And then CODA, when they routed to NYSE, they changed the NPID, but they keep these the same. So these would need to match what succession sent. So that's how FINRA keeps track when the NPID changes, right? Because when it changes to CODA, they go in their names because they have", "pol": "And then Coda, when they route it to NYSE, they change the MPID but keep these the same. So these would need to match what Succession sent. That's how FINRA keeps track when the MPID changes, right? Because when it goes through Coda, they use their own names.", "zh": "然后Coda在把订单路由到NYSE时会改MPID，但保持这些不变。所以这些需要和Succession发出的匹配。这就是MPID变化时FINRA用来追踪的方式，对吧？因为经过Coda时，他们会用自己的名义。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 458.99, "e": 482.2}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "You know, a certain they probably get certain tiers for their order flow if they go out of their name, right? So they change it from our names. They still report the original. So those folks, these is in. Yes, I believe so. I just want to change when. Yes.", "pol": "They probably get certain tiers for their order flow if it goes out under their name, right? So they change it from our names, but they still report the original. So those are the IDs they use? Yes, I believe so.", "zh": "如果订单流以他们的名义发出，他们大概能拿到某些费率层级，对吧？所以他们把我们的名义改掉，但仍然上报原始的标识。所以他们用的就是那些ID？是的，我相信是。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 482.52, "e": 502.92}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So it's FINRA's way of keeping track of who the original order came from, when the MDID is changing between different legs of the oracle.", "pol": "So it's FINRA's way of keeping track of who the original order came from, when the MPID is changing between different legs of the order.", "zh": "所以这是FINRA在MPID于订单不同环节之间发生变化时，用来追踪原始订单来源的方式。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 506.24, "e": 518.82}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "MCI, DBN, CODA, DAO, exchange, and so on. And we have a lot of reporting on how to track CODA generators, succession generators, and so on. Thank you.", "pol": "VCL, BCL, Coda, exchange, and so on — we have a lot of reporting on how to track Coda generators, Succession generators, and so on.", "zh": "VCL、BCL、Coda、交易所等等——关于如何追踪Coda生成器、Succession生成器之类，我们有很多上报。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 572.88, "e": 583.65}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "They are asking if you can send an email to ask a succession about this cat report. How they sent the file, about the format, the real-time, and the MTID, and all this.", "pol": "They're asking if you can send an email to ask Succession about this CAT report — how they send the file, the format, whether it's real time, the MTID, and all this.", "zh": "他们在问你能不能发邮件去问Succession关于这份CAT报告的事——他们怎么发文件、格式、是不是实时、MTID，以及所有这些。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 634.48, "e": 647.78}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "And then we can figure out how can we influence.", "pol": "And then we can figure out how we can influence it.", "zh": "然后我们就能想清楚我们能怎么去影响它。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 651.01, "e": 653.49}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "What does CAT identify a difference between the one succession generator and the one COVID generator? What's the consequence? Oh, what's the consequence if they don't match?", "pol": "What does CAT identify as a difference between the Succession-generated one and the Coda-generated one? What's the consequence if they don't match?", "zh": "CAT会识别出Succession生成的和Coda生成的之间有什么差异？如果不匹配会有什么后果？", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 724.14, "e": 736.42}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "You just need to I mean, I don't know what happens if you don't fix them, but you're supposed to fix them But if we don't fix them the order won't go through This is just a requirement by FINRA It need to match. Yeah, so the requirement by FINRA is that those three ID need to be matched", "pol": "You just need to fix them. I don't know what happens if you don't, but you're supposed to fix them. This is a FINRA requirement — those three IDs need to match.", "zh": "你只要把它们改对就行。我不知道不改会怎样，但你本来就该改。这是FINRA的要求——那三个ID必须匹配。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 739.13, "e": 763.17}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Well, the two first ones, I think. I don't know the specifics, but I think the MPID and the MPID doesn't matter. You still need to report what the MPID was and what you sent me. Why MPID doesn't matter? Because MPID is an active name that's associated with the order. And that changes between different languages.", "pol": "The first two, I think. I don't know the specifics, but the MPID doesn't matter — you still need to report what the MPID was. Why doesn't MPID matter? Because MPID is a firm name associated with the order, and that changes between different venues.", "zh": "我想是前两个。具体我不清楚，但MPID不重要——你仍然要上报当时的MPID是什么。为什么MPID不重要？因为MPID是与订单关联的公司名，在不同场所之间会变。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 763.37, "e": 788.29}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So, when we send your name on it, sometimes it might just go straight to the exchange in our name, right? But in other times, if we route it to CODA, CODA might change the MPID to their name because their name is associated with a certain key or a certain key or a certain key. But it doesn't really matter, right? MPID doesn't matter. It's the other IDs in there.", "pol": "When we send an order, sometimes it goes straight to the exchange under our name. But other times, if we route it to Coda, Coda might change the MPID to their name because their name is tied to a certain venue. But it doesn't really matter — MPID doesn't matter, it's the other IDs that do.", "zh": "我们发订单时，有时会以我们的名义直接到交易所。但有时如果路由给Coda，Coda可能会把MPID改成他们的名义，因为他们的名义绑定了某个场所。但这其实不重要——MPID不重要，重要的是另外那些ID。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 788.33, "e": 810.02}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Um, so Kat will throw out like a notification if", "pol": "So CAT will throw out a notification if...", "zh": "所以如果……CAT就会抛出一条通知。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 810.62, "e": 816.85}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "MPID doesn't matter, it's the first tool.", "pol": "MPID doesn't matter — it's the first two.", "zh": "MPID不重要——重要的是前两个。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 817.8, "e": 821.76}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "M-P-I-D, I-M-I-D, F-D-I-D. You watch it out. We'll answer your question.", "pol": "MPID, IMID, FDID. You asked about it — we'll answer your question.", "zh": "MPID、IMID、FDID。你问到的——我们会回答你。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 841.15, "e": 848.11}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "So if they don't match, who has the responsibility to fix it? We do. We have to fix it. Tickers? Yes. Not secession? Not to call that? No, we have to fix it. Or we have to call it? Or we may have to call that ET to fix it?", "pol": "So if they don't match, who's responsible for fixing it? We are. We have to fix it — not Succession, not Coda. Or do we have to call them to fix it?", "zh": "那如果不匹配，谁负责改？是我们。得我们来改——不是Succession，也不是Coda。还是说得打电话让他们改？", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 871.28, "e": 885.48}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "Can we like log into the cast or in the portal to see the Yeah difference compliance Compliance control", "pol": "Can we log into the CAT portal to see the differences? Is that compliance-controlled?", "zh": "我们能登录CAT门户去看差异吗？那是合规管控的吗？", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 901.25, "e": 912.67}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "Yeah, I mean, it's something that has been said for many years. Now, I think that the user generally sees the photo, and sees the photo. And then, looks like there are IMIDs, FDIDs that are left behind. So, it's like a third-order error. I think it's important to recognize that we need to reconciliate and that we need to make sure that we have the right tools.", "pol": "It's something that's been talked about for years. Users generally see the report and notice there are IMIDs and FDIDs left behind. So it's a kind of downstream error. I think it's important to recognize that we need to reconcile and make sure we have the right tools.", "zh": "这事已经说了好几年了。用户通常看报告时会发现有遗留的IMID和FDID。所以这算是一种下游错误。我认为关键是要认识到我们需要对账，并确保手上有合适的工具。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 937.45, "e": 968.6}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "What's the meaning of IMID and FDID? FDID is a number that's generated when an account is created and it's like permanently, it's a unique identifier for that specific account. The IMID is an ID and this is associated with a certain type of customer. So the IMID, yeah, it's unique identifier for account IMID is unique, yeah, unique identifier. This is a people.", "pol": "What do IMID and FDID mean? FDID is a number generated when an account is created — it's permanent, a unique identifier for that specific account. The IMID is an ID associated with a certain type of customer. So the FDID is a unique identifier for the account, and the IMID is a unique identifier for the person.", "zh": "IMID和FDID是什么意思？FDID是开户时生成的号码——它是永久的，是该特定账户的唯一标识。IMID是与某类客户关联的ID。所以FDID是账户的唯一标识，IMID是人的唯一标识。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 1012.6, "e": 1039.5}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "No, so you succession, do you essentially report on your big map, that's why when there's a break it's our response.", "pol": "Succession essentially reports on our behalf, which is why when there's a break, it's our responsibility.", "zh": "Succession基本上是代表我们上报的，所以一旦出现对账异常，责任在我们。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 1050.24, "e": 1057.64}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "It's not related to order though, right?", "pol": "It's not related to the order, though, right?", "zh": "不过这跟订单本身没关系，对吧？", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 1101.03, "e": 1102.91}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "No, no, no. It's more just you need to report it every time an order is sent. But it's not a trade perspective. It's more like once the order is complete. It's when the order is routed. When the order is routed from member to succession to hold up.", "pol": "No — you need to report it every time an order is sent. But it's not from a trade perspective; it's when the order is routed — when the order is routed from us to Succession, or whoever.", "zh": "不——每次发订单都要上报。但不是从成交的角度，而是在订单被路由时——当订单从我们这里路由到Succession或别的什么方时。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 1105.89, "e": 1125.34}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "Regarding this mPID, is that the consolidated ID? Because VCL has a lot of customers, right? Yeah. Each of them has their own upon ID? Yes. And we have our VCL, VACON ID, which one? So, it would only be...", "pol": "Regarding this MPID, is that the consolidated ID? Because VCL has a lot of customers, right? Each of them has their own ID, and we have our VCL ID — which one would it be?", "zh": "关于这个MPID，那是合并后的ID吗？因为VCL有很多客户对吧？他们每个人都有自己的ID，我们也有我们VCL的ID——到底用哪一个？", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 1188.31, "e": 1210.95}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So, for us, it would be our account ID, right? Just our one account ID, because it's the one that we're routing, right? Business just receiving it, it doesn't matter from the customer. It's us. You report when you route it, right? It was the big one.", "pol": "For us, it would be our firm ID — the one we're routing with. The receiving side is just receiving it; it doesn't matter which customer. It's us reporting when we route it.", "zh": "对我们来说，就是我们公司的ID——我们用来路由的那个。接收方只是接收，不管是哪个客户。是我们在路由时上报。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 1212.55, "e": 1229.21}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So, like, whenever we create a VCL account in our back office, it generates a unique identifier at the ID. This is unique to this account specifically. So, every time that an order is routed in this account, we report this.", "pol": "Whenever we create a VCL account in our back office, it generates a unique FDID. This is unique to this account specifically, so every time an order is routed for this account, we report this FDID.", "zh": "每当我们在后台创建一个VCL账户时，就会生成一个唯一的FDID。它专属于这个账户，所以每次为这个账户路由订单时，我们都上报这个FDID。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 1309.92, "e": 1332.66}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "F. D. I. And then that shows that it was specifically this account, right? Because who knows? Maybe another broker dealer happens to have the same account number. This is like the unique identifier only associated with this specific. This is more like a. Yeah, well, it's it's an account I. type specifically to this customer account. Yeah.", "pol": "And that shows it was specifically this account — because maybe another broker-dealer happens to have the same account number. This is the unique identifier associated only with this specific account; it's an account ID specific to this customer account.", "zh": "这就表明具体是这个账户——因为说不定别的券商刚好有相同的账号。这是只与这个特定账户关联的唯一标识；它是专属于该客户账户的账户ID。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 1333.08, "e": 1359.11}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "I'm pretty sure imid will be something like it'll be something very simple like uh like individual or customer the relationship between im and fdid is that one one for one or no no imid it's i think it's usually just like one character it'll be something like individual", "pol": "I'm pretty sure IMID will be something simple like 'individual' or 'customer'. Is the relationship between IMID and FDID one-to-one? No — IMID is usually just one character, something like 'individual'.", "zh": "我很确定IMID会是很简单的东西，比如“个人”或“客户”。IMID和FDID是一一对应吗？不是——IMID通常就一个字符，类似“个人”这种。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 1386.99, "e": 1413.02}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "or like broker dealer or something like that. Right, the FDID is the like real identifier. It's more like the type of order flow, I guess, this would be like a, like see how this, this one has different FDID below.", "pol": "or like broker-dealer or something like that. Right, the FDID is the real identifier. It's more like the type of order flow, I guess — see how this one has a different FDID below.", "zh": "或者像券商之类的。对，FDID才是真正的标识。我想它更像是订单流的类型——看这个，下面有一个不同的FDID。", "tp": "订单标识(FDID/IMID/MPID)", "s": 1413.9, "e": 1431.95}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "We need a sample of this class reporting and we can implement that.", "pol": "We need a sample of this CAT reporting, then we can implement that.", "zh": "我们需要一份这个CAT上报的样本，然后就能着手实现了。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 1472.25, "e": 1481.16}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "Yes, we have to fix the data, right? Yes, we have to fix it, we have to fix it. We have to have a good data collection, so that the data is able to be used as a velocity, and the data is able to be used as a velocity.", "pol": "Yes, we have to fix the data. We need good data collection so that the data can be used by Velocity.", "zh": "是的，我们必须把数据修正好。我们需要良好的数据采集，这样数据才能被Velocity使用。", "tp": "清算与后台", "s": 1525.86, "e": 1552.18}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Well, I mean, how would the heavy orders get to you? There has to be fixed here, right?", "pol": "Well, how would the bulk of orders get to you? There has to be a FIX connection here, right?", "zh": "那大批订单是怎么到你们那里的？这里总得有个FIX连接吧？", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 1601.64, "e": 1606.46}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "And then, I mean, if you have something between like your app, I mean, this is coming from the app, right? Yes. So, yeah, whatever is connected. Yeah, cool. Connected to the app. We have a home. Mm-hmm. In the world. Yeah.", "pol": "And if you have something between, like your app — this is coming from the app, right? Yes. So whatever is connected to the app.", "zh": "如果你们中间还有别的，比如你们的App——这是从App来的，对吧？是的。所以就是接到App上的那些。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 1609.85, "e": 1629.45}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Do we have other ones? Oh yeah, they would also be fixed in, yes. Every one of them.", "pol": "Do we have other ones? Oh yeah, they'd also need to be FIXed in — every one of them.", "zh": "我们还有别的吗？哦对，它们也都要通过FIX接进来——每一个都要。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 1652.15, "e": 1657.41}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Yeah, it's really completely removed. So session are the customers will also need to do so. They all a lot of them use traffic So you would only actually be one session from traffic", "pol": "Yeah, it's completely removed. So the customers will also need to connect — a lot of them use Traffic. So you'd actually only need one session from Traffic.", "zh": "是的，它被完全移除了。所以客户也需要接入——他们很多人用Traffic。所以你其实只需要来自Traffic的一个会话。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 1687.2, "e": 1698.5}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "But Trafix, yesterday you said... Yeah, they do two things. Trafix is two separate things. One of them is just a trading front-end, like the app, kind of like your app. The other part is the whole on-mass backup thing. That's completely unrelated. But our customers today, we use Trafix as a trading front-end, like our whole, like it's like our whole app. We have one session from Trafix front-end to succession.", "pol": "But Traffic — yesterday you said... Yeah, they do two things. Traffic is two separate things. One is just a trading front end, like the app, kind of like your app. The other part is the whole OMS backup thing, which is completely unrelated. But today our customers use Traffic as a trading front end — it's like our whole app. We have one session from the Traffic front end to Succession.", "zh": "但Traffic——你昨天说……对，他们做两件事。Traffic其实是两个独立的东西。一个只是交易前端，像App，有点像你们的App。另一部分是整套OMS备份，那完全不相关。但如今我们的客户把Traffic当交易前端用——就相当于我们整个App。我们有一条从Traffic前端到Succession的会话。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 1700.97, "e": 1725.75}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So if we're to replace succession, we would need one session from traffic's front end to the GTS.", "pol": "So if we're going to replace Succession, we'd need one session from Traffic's front end to GTS.", "zh": "所以如果我们要替换Succession，就需要一条从Traffic前端到GTS的会话。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 1725.95, "e": 1731.07}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "And then all of our customers who use traffic, they can all come over to that one section. So I don't need one for each. Thanks.", "pol": "And then all of our customers who use Traffic can all come over to that one session. So I don't need one for each.", "zh": "然后所有用Traffic的客户都可以走那一条会话。所以我不需要每个客户一条。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 1732.88, "e": 1746.07}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Well, it depends on how you want to do it. Where are they coming from? Do you have one system for the app?", "pol": "Well, it depends on how you want to do it. Where are they coming from? Do you have one system for the app?", "zh": "这取决于你想怎么做。它们从哪里来？你们App是用一个系统吗？", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 1746.76, "e": 1754.27}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Just like if there are different systems So if there are different systems, there's two ways we can do it. You can have a separate one for each customer One for someone for Singapore one. We separate things. Yes, or if you have If you have a different system that it manages all of the awkward then we can then you can do one", "pol": "If there are different systems, there are two ways we can do it. You can have a separate one for each customer — one for someone, one for Singapore. Or, if you have one system that manages all of the orders, then you can do just one.", "zh": "如果是不同的系统，我们有两种做法。你可以给每个客户单独一条——一个给某人，一个给新加坡。或者，如果你有一个统一管理所有订单的系统，那就可以只做一条。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 1768.16, "e": 1789.15}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "from whatever the message is to BTS. BTS, yeah. Not traffic. No, no, no. So traffic's, so traffic's, I don't even know because our other customers, they're unrelated to BTS or songs or anything. They use traffic and all of their orders in the traffic's on this before it comes to us. So it only needs one section. Yeah. Yeah, I don't think we're in that phase. So it'd be separated?", "pol": "from whatever the message is, to GTS. GTS, yeah, not Traffic. Because our other customers are unrelated to GTS or SoftTech or anything — they use Traffic, and all of their orders go through Traffic before they come to us. So it only needs one session. I don't think we're in that phase yet. So it'd be separated?", "zh": "从任何消息，到GTS。是GTS，不是Traffic。因为我们的其他客户跟GTS或SoftTech什么的都无关——他们用Traffic，所有订单都先经过Traffic再到我们。所以只需要一条会话。我觉得我们还没到那个阶段。所以要分开？", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 1791.33, "e": 1817.95}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So you would do one for someone, one for Singapore.", "pol": "So you'd do one for SoftTech, one for Singapore.", "zh": "所以你会做一条给SoftTech，一条给新加坡。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 1818.75, "e": 1820.83}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "We have a lot of other things that we have to do. We have to make sure that all the other routes are safe. We have to make sure that we are not using Linux. We have to make sure that we don't have traffic. We have to make sure that we don't have to back up.", "pol": "We have a lot of other things to do. We have to make sure all the other routes are safe, make sure we're not relying on just Linux, make sure Traffic is in place, and make sure we have a backup.", "zh": "我们还有很多别的事要做。要确保所有其他路由都安全，确保不是只靠Linux，确保Traffic就位，并确保有备份。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 1999.66, "e": 2020.17}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "We've never seen traffic before is that possible if you can demonstrate something like you have a system", "pol": "We've never seen Traffic before — would it be possible for you to demonstrate the system?", "zh": "我们以前没见过Traffic——你能演示一下这个系统吗？", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 2054.19, "e": 2062.29}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "All right, this is what like, 1 of our customers would see if they wanted to input in order to traffic. So. I mean, this is what the system looks like, right? I can, I can see my orders here. I can put orders here. It's all connected to Bloomberg. Yeah. I don't have market data right now, but I could.", "pol": "All right, this is what one of our customers would see if they wanted to input an order into Traffic. This is what the system looks like. I can see my orders here, I can enter orders here. It's all connected to Bloomberg. I don't have market data right now, but I could.", "zh": "好，这就是我们的客户想在Traffic里下单时会看到的界面。系统大概就长这样。我在这里能看到我的订单，也能在这里录入订单。它全部接到了彭博。我现在没有行情数据，但可以接上。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 2078.61, "e": 2105.37}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "It's basically just an order entry system. They say you can place order on the system. Yes. And it's connected to Bloomberg for all the market data. And then if I go to succession, these are inbound sessions. What's the relationship between succession and...", "pol": "It's basically just an order entry system — you can place orders on it, and it's connected to Bloomberg for all the market data. And then if I go to Succession, these are inbound sessions. What's the relationship between Succession and...?", "zh": "它基本上就是个订单录入系统——你可以在上面下单，并且接了彭博获取所有行情。然后如果我进到Succession，这些是入站会话。Succession和……之间是什么关系？", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 2105.56, "e": 2127.09}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "They're not related at all. They're just, they're completely separate entities, but our customers like to use this order entry system that Trafix provides. And so because- Because the session doesn't have- Yeah, they don't really have a good order entry system, right? So as you can see, this is one of our clients, like there's a fixed session here from Trafix.", "pol": "They're not related at all — they're completely separate entities. But our customers like to use this order entry system that Traffic provides, because Succession doesn't really have a good order entry system, right? So as you can see, this is one of our clients — there's a FIX session here from Traffic.", "zh": "它们完全没关系——是彻底独立的实体。但我们的客户喜欢用Traffic提供的这个订单录入系统，因为Succession确实没有好用的录入系统，对吧？所以你看，这是我们的一个客户——这里有一条来自Traffic的FIX会话。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 2129.18, "e": 2155.87}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "to succession. So yeah, if we're going to replace succession, because the order, well, succession issued a session for trappics to connect to. Okay, so special issue of traffic. Because succession in this case is the receiving party of the order, right? So, whoever's the receiving party, they host the session. They bring it up.", "pol": "...to Succession. So if we're going to replace Succession — Succession issued a session for Traffic to connect to, because Succession in this case is the receiving party of the order. So whoever's the receiving party hosts the session; they bring it up.", "zh": "……到Succession。所以如果我们要替换Succession——是Succession开了一条会话让Traffic来连，因为在这里Succession是订单的接收方。谁是接收方谁就托管会话，由他们把会话建立起来。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 2156.48, "e": 2180.78}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "out they're the ones listening for for orders and listen to traffic and now and then traffics is connected to that session and then whenever i send an order here it sends fixed message over that session to succession and then succession routes it to and so if we're going to replace succession", "pol": "They're the ones listening for orders. Traffic is connected to that session, and whenever I send an order here, it sends a FIX message over that session to Succession, and then Succession routes it onward. So if we're going to replace Succession...", "zh": "他们是监听订单的一方。Traffic连到那条会话，每当我在这里发单，它就通过那条会话向Succession发一条FIX消息，然后Succession再往下路由。所以如果我们要替换Succession……", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 2180.82, "e": 2201.31}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "for our clients that we have, using traffic's front end. Just thinking. You'd like to think of the customer.", "pol": "...for our clients that use Traffic's front end. Just thinking — you'd want to consider the customer.", "zh": "……对于用Traffic前端的那些客户。只是在想——你得把客户考虑进去。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 2201.97, "e": 2215.6}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "No, not there yet. So it's just like, it'd be like, it's like, it'd be another one here. It's just, you can ignore that it's traffic. That's what's confusing because we just try these for two different things. Just think of it as another fixed session that would need to come in.", "pol": "It's not there yet. It would be like another one here. You can ignore that it's Traffic — that's what's confusing, because we use Traffic for two different things. Just think of it as another FIX session that would need to come in.", "zh": "还没到那一步。这里会再有一条。你可以忽略它是Traffic这件事——这正是让人困惑的地方，因为我们把Traffic用在两种不同用途上。就把它当成另一条需要接入的FIX会话就行。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 2239.29, "e": 2256.28}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Hang on, it's still a backup for a success. Yeah, so yeah, so that's where it gets confusing.", "pol": "It's still a backup for Succession. That's where it gets confusing.", "zh": "它仍然是Succession的备份。这就是容易混淆的地方。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2279.61, "e": 2286.88}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So the entire thing, we have it also set up with traffic. Okay. So you can just ignore this. We have the entire thing set up with traffic also, but we never use it. It's only a backup. So you can just replace either of these, right? But these are separate.", "pol": "We have the entire thing set up with Traffic as well. You can just ignore this — we set the whole thing up with Traffic too, but we never use it; it's only a backup. So you can replace either of these, but these are separate.", "zh": "我们也用Traffic把整套都搭好了。你可以忽略这个——我们同样用Traffic搭了一整套，只是从不用它，它只是备份。所以这两个你替换哪个都行，但它们是分开的。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2304.42, "e": 2331.6}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "In this instance, if we're using Trafix here, we would have a traffic session into Trafix from a separate Trafix.", "pol": "In this instance, if we're using Traffic here, we would have a Traffic session into Traffic from a separate Traffic.", "zh": "在这种情况下，如果这里用Traffic，我们会从一个独立的Traffic再建一条到Traffic的会话。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2332.33, "e": 2340.38}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So what we have to do right now, we've already done it with graphics.", "pol": "So what we need to do right now — we've already done it with GTS.", "zh": "所以我们现在要做的——我们已经用GTS做过一遍了。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2351.16, "e": 2358.7}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Something has to come back into it. No, so basically actually traffic can do at least", "pol": "Something has to come back into it. Basically, Traffic can do at least that.", "zh": "总得有东西再接回去。基本上，Traffic至少能做到这一点。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2369.86, "e": 2377.79}, {"sp": "王发壮", "en": "So there's a possible traffic is created by successful.", "pol": "So it's possible the Traffic backup is created by Succession.", "zh": "所以有可能这个Traffic备份是由Succession创建的。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2431.36, "e": 2435.34}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "So you mentioned that traffic is a backup of suspension, right? So let's say if we have an order from the sale customer, and so such a result. Yes. It goes to traffic. Well, no. So we set this all up in UAT so far. All we would need to do that is", "pol": "You mentioned Traffic is a backup for Succession, right? So let's say we get an order from the sales customer and it goes to Traffic. Well, no. So far we've set this all up in UAT. All we'd need to do is add another session.", "zh": "你提到Traffic是Succession的备份，对吧？那假设我们收到销售客户的订单，它走到Traffic。呃，不是这样。目前我们都是在UAT里搭的。我们要做的只是再加一条会话。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2452.64, "e": 2475.64}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "We would have another session that would, we would have these sessions pointed to traffic. We haven't issued those yet. I guess it would be to from here to here. So, all we have to do is ask traffic. To give you give you those sessions and then if succession, we're down on BCL, send them down that session instead. So, sorry, start that again if we say, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.", "pol": "We'd point these sessions to Traffic. We haven't issued those yet. All we have to do is ask Traffic to give you those sessions, and then if Succession were down, BCL would send them down that session instead.", "zh": "我们会把这些会话指向Traffic。这些我们还没开出来。我们要做的就是请Traffic把那些会话给你们，然后一旦Succession宕机，BCL就改从那条会话发送。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2475.98, "e": 2503.49}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Yeah, so we have this whole thing set up as succession, right? We've set it all up with traffic. The only thing we haven't done is have VCL connect the effects to traffic yet. We're in UAT right now, but we can at any point issue guys a UAT session. You guys can start testing that, and then we can issue production sessions and then you guys can test that as well.", "pol": "We have this whole thing set up as Succession, and we've set it all up with Traffic too. The only thing we haven't done is have VCL connect the FIX to Traffic yet. We're in UAT right now, but we can issue you a UAT session at any time. You can start testing that, then we can issue production sessions and you can test those too.", "zh": "我们把整套按Succession搭好了，也用Traffic全搭了一套。唯一还没做的是让VCL把FIX连到Traffic。我们现在在UAT阶段，但随时可以给你们发UAT会话。你们可以先测，然后我们再发生产会话，你们也可以测。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2504.3, "e": 2524.57}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "But in, once that's done, if succession went down, your accession to succession would drop, right? So then you guys would have the traffic sessions available as well. You guys could route to the traffic session instead. And then we have the entire thing mirrored, but instead of succession, it's traffic.", "pol": "Once that's done, if Succession went down, your connection to Succession would drop, right? Then you'd also have the Traffic sessions available — you could route to the Traffic session instead. And then we'd have the entire thing mirrored, but instead of Succession, it's Traffic.", "zh": "一旦搞定，如果Succession宕机，你们到Succession的连接就会断，对吧？那时你们也有Traffic会话可用——可以改路由到Traffic会话。这样整套就被镜像了，只不过不是Succession，而是Traffic。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2525.36, "e": 2546.08}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "What about for existing orders? Or is this backup only for the new orders? This would be backup for new orders. The existing orders that we have got. There's nothing to do about that. How about if the new order goes back? It would cancel.", "pol": "What about existing orders? Or is this backup only for new orders? This would be a backup for new orders. For the existing orders we already have, there's nothing to do about that. What if a new order goes back? It would cancel.", "zh": "那已有的订单呢？还是说这个备份只针对新订单？这是针对新订单的备份。对于已经在手的存量订单，无能为力。如果新订单被退回怎么办？它会被取消。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2591.08, "e": 2604.09}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "This would be like, you only switch the traffic, it's like the worst case scenario. Like everything is down. Everything is down. Because if you think about it, there's only one point of contact between VCL and all of this, and it's right here. So if this went down, then everything would be down essentially, right?", "pol": "You'd only switch to Traffic in the worst-case scenario — like everything is down. Because if you think about it, there's only one point of contact between VCL and all of this, and it's right here. So if this went down, everything would essentially be down, right?", "zh": "你只会在最坏的情况下才切到Traffic——比如一切都挂了。因为想想看，VCL和这一切之间只有一个接触点，就在这儿。所以一旦这里挂了，基本上就全挂了，对吧？", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2611.07, "e": 2635.84}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "right so that's why we have traffic and that's why you build a new session yes just doing just in case yeah i mean ideally we would never have to use", "pol": "That's why we have Traffic, and that's why you build a new session — just in case. Ideally, we'd never have to use it.", "zh": "这就是我们要有Traffic的原因，也是你要再搭一条新会话的原因——以防万一。理想情况下我们永远都用不上它。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2635.96, "e": 2645.86}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "send this traffic on production, right? Only in UAT. Only in UAT, yeah. We can, we can issue a UAT session. You guys can pass it.", "pol": "We wouldn't send this Traffic to production yet — only in UAT. We can issue a UAT session, and you guys can test it.", "zh": "我们暂时不会把这个Traffic放到生产——只在UAT。我们可以发一条UAT会话，你们来测。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2669.24, "e": 2677.89}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "The issue of traffic is important, and of course, we are seeing it in China, Singapore and Hong Kong. We already have a traffic issue in Hong Kong, so we are people who are now in traffic, and now we are able to access an AP", "pol": "The Traffic issue is important, and we're seeing it in China, Singapore and Hong Kong. We already have Traffic in Hong Kong, so now we're able to access it via an API.", "zh": "Traffic这个问题很重要，在中国、新加坡和香港我们都遇到了。香港这边我们已经上了Traffic，所以现在能通过API接入了。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 2695.82, "e": 2719.88}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "Yeah, I have a sample from the sixth part of them. Just in general, you know, in general, we have the one for code. Yeah, I have the one for dash, and I have the one for succession on n. Do I have the one for mostly?", "pol": "I have a sample from the FIX part of them. In general, we have the one for Coda, I have the one for dash, and I have the one for Succession. Do I have the one for the rest?", "zh": "他们FIX那部分的样本我有。总的来说，Coda的我们有，dash的我有，Succession的我也有。剩下那个我有吗？", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 2822.11, "e": 2843.82}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "I can get this discussion fixed back. That would be helpful because when you guys are Connecting new users. That's kind of the model You need your own protocol", "pol": "If I can get this session fixed, that would be helpful — because when you're connecting new users, that's the model: you need your own protocol.", "zh": "如果能把这条会话弄好会很有帮助——因为当你们接新用户时就是这个模式：你们需要自己的协议。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 2846.06, "e": 2870.49}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "And for the SEC pretrench head.", "pol": "And for the SEC pre-check part.", "zh": "还有SEC预检查那部分。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 2874.93, "e": 2881.13}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So, what will we do on this, as they say, Richard? Well, I have a description, so I have examples of the ones that Succession has, and then I think Kevin's going to talk a little bit about just all the regulations.", "pol": "So what will we do on this, Richard? Well, I have descriptions and examples of the ones that Succession has, and then I think Kevin's going to talk a bit about all the regulations.", "zh": "那这个我们怎么做，Richard？我这边有Succession那些的说明和例子，然后我想Kevin会讲一点所有相关法规。", "tp": "监管上报/CAT", "s": 2917.4, "e": 2934.05}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "We developed a copy to synchronize the trade execution information to velocity.", "pol": "We developed a drop copy to synchronize the trade execution information to Velocity.", "zh": "我们做了一个Drop Copy，把成交执行信息同步给Velocity。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3053.92, "e": 3062.28}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "So, in terms of settlement and clearing, they received something, right? Yes. What if we change perception to DDS? What would it convert to? Velocity? They would get...", "pol": "So in terms of settlement and clearing, they receive something too, right? Yes. What if we change the session to GTS? What would it feed into — Velocity? They would get...", "zh": "那么在清算与交收方面，他们也会收到东西，对吧？是的。如果我们把这条会话改成GTS呢？它会接到哪里——Velocity？他们会拿到……", "tp": "清算与后台", "s": 3286.53, "e": 3303.16}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "End-of-day CSV files. So every order, every trade that goes through the system is generated in CSV format with the velocity account number so that they can load into their office at the end of the day. And then in real time, they send execution messages to velocity. Yes, so it's", "pol": "End-of-day CSV files. Every order, every trade that goes through the system is generated in CSV format with the Velocity account number, so they can load it into their office at the end of the day. And then in real time, they send execution messages to Velocity.", "zh": "日终CSV文件。通过系统的每个订单、每笔成交都会以CSV格式生成，带上Velocity的账户号，这样他们在收盘时能导入到自己那边。然后实时地，他们把执行消息发给Velocity。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3304.79, "e": 3325.63}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "it's similar to how it would send them to like soft tech or to uh or intel yeah so just the execution that's because since we route our workers away like we route to kona velocity doesn't see what we're doing throughout the day so they just want to draw a copy so they can monitor what we're doing during the day that's it what do we need to do if we change", "pol": "It's similar to how we'd send them to SoftTech or Intelliclear — just the execution. Since we route our orders away, like to Coda, Velocity doesn't see what we're doing throughout the day, so they just want a drop copy to monitor what we're doing during the day. What do we need to do if we change?", "zh": "这类似于我们发给SoftTech或Intelliclear的方式——只是执行信息。因为我们把订单路由出去（比如给Coda），Velocity看不到我们一天里在做什么，所以他们只想要一份Drop Copy来监控我们日内的动作。如果我们要改，需要做什么？", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3326.92, "e": 3352.84}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So you would need to set up a drop copy session to velocity for this execution.", "pol": "So you'd need to set up a drop copy session to Velocity for this execution.", "zh": "所以你需要为这个执行设置一条到Velocity的Drop Copy会话。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3353.27, "e": 3359.15}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "and then like ERD file.", "pol": "...and then an EOD CSV file.", "zh": "……然后再来一个日终CSV文件。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3373.01, "e": 3374.45}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "So did they ask Henry that you do trade to file to velocity. Tanya.", "pol": "So did they ask whether you send the trade file to Velocity, Tanya?", "zh": "那他们有没有问，你们是否把成交文件发给Velocity，Tanya？", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3392.02, "e": 3402.57}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Is it enough? Is that real-time or enough? It's end of day, it's end of day. It's not real-time? Drop copy is real-time, file is end of day.", "pol": "Is it real-time or end of day? It's end of day. Not real-time? The drop copy is real-time; the file is end of day.", "zh": "是实时的还是日终的？是日终的。不是实时的？Drop Copy是实时的，文件是日终的。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3413.42, "e": 3420.89}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "Do we have a sample of you already? Can you send us welcome?", "pol": "Do you already have a sample? Can you send us one?", "zh": "你们已经有样本了吗？能发我们一份吗？", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3464.9, "e": 3469.83}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "Is that generated from the session system? Yes. Should I? And then it's dropped on SFT now. Oh, SFT.", "pol": "Is that generated from the Succession system? Yes. And then it's dropped to SoftTech now. Oh, SoftTech.", "zh": "那是从Succession系统生成的吗？是的。然后现在会推送到SoftTech。哦，SoftTech。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3479.48, "e": 3488.85}, {"sp": "蒋灿", "en": "I think we can have a job copy. We have a success. We can have a job copy and have a real success. A real success. We'll have a job copy. We'll have a real success. Thank you.", "pol": "I think we can have a drop copy. We have Succession. We can have a drop copy for it.", "zh": "我觉得我们可以做一份Drop Copy。我们有Succession。可以为它做一份Drop Copy。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3492.92, "e": 3506.96}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "So, real-time, you can use real-time to draw a copy of the book, and you can use it in real-time, right?", "pol": "So in real time, you can use it to drop a copy of the book, and use it in real time, right?", "zh": "所以实时地，你可以用它把订单簿做一份Drop Copy，并实时使用，对吧？", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3533.01, "e": 3540.13}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "If you want to use GTS in real-time, you can use GTS in real-time to copy real-time data from real-time.", "pol": "If you want it in real time, you can use GTS to produce the real-time drop copy data.", "zh": "如果你要实时的，可以用GTS来产出实时的Drop Copy数据。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3542.29, "e": 3551.29}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "I'll pitch for that, Thoreau, if that's okay.", "pol": "I'll pitch for that, if that's okay.", "zh": "如果可以的话，我来推动这个。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 3556.97, "e": 3558.49}, {"sp": "Speaker 4", "en": "I don't think it's time for that.", "pol": "I don't think it's time for that yet.", "zh": "我觉得现在还不到时候。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 3582.48, "e": 3585.24}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "And then it will be the same thing. We also do drop copies to stop that Same thing fix real-time drops. If all of these would sit in the same place, right? There's drop to velocity drop to soft tech Drop to our Intel clear. Oh There's EOD CSV files for all of those as well. So all of those", "pol": "And then it's the same thing — we also do drop copies to all of them. Same thing: FIX real-time drops. All of these would sit in the same place: a drop to Velocity, a drop to SoftTech, a drop to our Intelliclear. And there are EOD CSV files for all of those as well.", "zh": "然后都是一样的——我们也向所有这些方做Drop Copy。一样的：FIX实时推送。这些都会放在同一处：推给Velocity、推给SoftTech、推给我们的Intelliclear。而且这些也都各有日终CSV文件。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3592.55, "e": 3616.17}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "And also to soft type into there. Yes, yeah. So it would be basically this and this times three. Interclear or soft type? Yeah, yeah. Just in the velocity, interclear or soft type. Daily the job copy the real time.", "pol": "And also to SoftTech. So it would basically be this times three — Velocity, Intelliclear and SoftTech: the daily file and the real-time drop copy.", "zh": "还有推给SoftTech。所以基本就是这个乘以三——Velocity、Intelliclear和SoftTech：每日文件加实时Drop Copy。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3616.62, "e": 3643.76}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Yeah, yeah. But you guys said if you're using GTS, you have the EMS, right? Yes. So you can ignore that. So we wouldn't need links tonight.", "pol": "But you guys said if you're using GTS, you have the EMS, right? Yes. So you can ignore that — we wouldn't need those links.", "zh": "但你们说过，如果用GTS，你们就有EMS，对吧？是的。所以那个可以忽略——我们就不需要那些连接了。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 3686.54, "e": 3702.86}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "The real-time job copy velocity is the end of the trade file. So you have to weigh the velocity. So you can see the real-time velocity. So you can see the real-time job copy velocity. So you can see the real-time job copy velocity is the end of the trade file.", "pol": "The real-time drop copy from Velocity is the end-of-day trade file. So with Velocity, you can see the real-time drop copy, which is the end-of-day trade file.", "zh": "来自Velocity的实时Drop Copy就是日终成交文件。所以有了Velocity，你就能看到那份实时Drop Copy，也就是日终成交文件。", "tp": "Drop Copy与日终文件", "s": 3741.38, "e": 3760.93}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Can we have a sample for it?", "pol": "Can we have a sample for it?", "zh": "能给我们一份样本吗？", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 3773.05, "e": 3778.61}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "What do you think about China's We'll talk about that. Finish.", "pol": "We'll talk about that later. That's it for now.", "zh": "这个我们回头再谈。先到这里。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 3797.09, "e": 3820.94}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "If we have traffic, we don't... Correct, they have all that functionality built in, so you don't need links.", "pol": "If we have Traffic — correct, they have all that functionality built in, so you don't need those links.", "zh": "如果我们有Traffic——对，他们把这些功能都内置了，所以你不需要那些连接。", "tp": "备份容灾(Traffic)", "s": 3939.24, "e": 3945.87}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "I mean, I guess the only optimization then would be, I guess, how you set up the free trade risk controls.", "pol": "I guess the only optimization then would be how you set up the pre-trade risk controls.", "zh": "我想那唯一的优化点，就是你怎么设置交易前风控。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 3993.98, "e": 3999.7}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "It's nice if the OMS has like full visibility into logs. Yeah, like looking being able to look in order and look at the logs easily. Just, you know, that's just like UI related stuff that makes it easier to do our job. To identify problems, right? Okay. Because then if I'm using this system, my job will be to monitor and solve problems.", "pol": "It's nice if the OMS has full visibility into logs — being able to look at an order and its logs easily. It's UI-related stuff that makes it easier to do our job and identify problems. Because if I'm using this system, my job will be to monitor and solve problems.", "zh": "如果OMS对日志有完整的可见性就很好——能方便地查看一个订单及其日志。这类偏UI的东西能让我们更容易开展工作、定位问题。因为我用这个系统时，我的工作就是监控并解决问题。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 4003.54, "e": 4031.47}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So being able to identify problems like looking at the fix, looking at the drop copy, those are important things to think about.", "pol": "So being able to identify problems — like looking at the FIX and looking at the drop copy — those are important things to think about.", "zh": "所以能定位问题——比如看FIX、看Drop Copy——这些都是需要重点考虑的。", "tp": "FIX会话与连通", "s": 4032.26, "e": 4038.89}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "Maybe we can do a demonstration for you.", "pol": "Maybe we can do a demonstration for you.", "zh": "也许我们可以给你们做个演示。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 4057.88, "e": 4068.41}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So back-office clearing, the one we don't have is our interaction with cost-building, such as velocity and BMO.", "pol": "So for back-office clearing, the one we don't have is our interaction with the custodian, such as Velocity and BMO.", "zh": "所以在后台清算方面，我们缺的是与托管方的对接，比如Velocity和BMO。", "tp": "清算与后台", "s": 4105.7, "e": 4113.21}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "So, yeah, you would need file for the backup. You would need to be able to inject data from both of them. Yes. Yeah. Also, eventually, if we become or when we become members, you guys would need to be able to connect your back office. D2C.", "pol": "So yeah, you'd need a file for the back office. You'd need to be able to inject data from both of them. Also, eventually — when we become DTC members — you'd need to be able to connect your back office to DTC.", "zh": "所以是的，后台需要一个文件。你需要能从这两者注入数据。另外，最终——当我们成为DTC会员时——你需要能把后台连到DTC。", "tp": "清算与后台", "s": 4117.05, "e": 4143.69}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "So how can we deal with this?", "pol": "So how can we deal with this?", "zh": "那我们该怎么处理这个？", "tp": "清算与后台", "s": 4186.53, "e": 4187.97}, {"sp": "Speaker 2", "en": "What velocity sometimes. The corporate action file. Yeah, we can.", "pol": "That's what Velocity sometimes gives us — the corporate action file. Yeah, we can.", "zh": "那正是Velocity有时给我们的——公司行动文件。是的，我们可以。", "tp": "清算与后台", "s": 4191.08, "e": 4200.07}, {"sp": "陈淑华", "en": "Yeah, that's quite a lot.", "pol": "Yeah, that's quite a lot.", "zh": "是的，这确实不少。", "tp": "系统演示/其他", "s": 4311.17, "e": 4322.77}]}]};
